{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And they told him all the words of Joseph</b> — It appears to me, according to the plain sense, that it was never told to Jacob all the days of his life that his sons sold Joseph, but rather he thought that he had wandered lost in the field and those who found him took him and sold him to Egypt, because his brothers did not wish to tell him their sin, all the more so since they feared for themselves lest he become wrathful and curse them as he did to Reuben and Simeon and Levi (Genesis 49:3–7). And Joseph, in his good discipline, did not wish to tell him. Therefore it is said, \"So you shall say to Joseph: Please bear now the transgression of your brothers and their sin, for they did evil to you\" — and the matter continues. Now, if Jacob had known this matter, it would have been fitting for them, when their father was near death, to entreat him to command Joseph directly from his own mouth, for he would show him favor and not disregard his word, and they would not have been in danger and would not have needed to fabricate words from their own hearts. For it is not possible that they would have devised the matter by themselves, since Jacob was the one who would need to address Joseph — but rather, they would have said to Jacob himself: \"Our father, forgive us, for we sinned against our brother; and now, command him, we pray you, that he bear our transgression.\" And Joseph too, had he heard it from his father, would have been bound to forgive them wholeheartedly and to sustain them willingly. But as it is, since he commanded him through them, it is as though Joseph needed to hear it from their mouths, and this is the way of one who fears Elohim — to be reconciled with his brother through an intermediary. And the verse says, \"and he spoke kindly to them\" (Genesis 50:21), meaning that he reassured them and spoke to their hearts."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text as supplied ends mid-argument with the word דברים. I have rendered only the text provided, but it appears to end abruptly; the full Ramban likely continues beyond what was given. I have translated the provided portion and not speculated on what follows."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:34.429932647Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}